 "doc": "documentation/C4P2_DESIGN.md §4.1/§6, TECHNICAL_ARCHITECTURE §12.1/§12.8/§12.9 — optional finds at the Karsk locomotive depot (scenes/levels/L_C4P2_Karsk.tscn, Story scenes L_C4P2_KarskA and L_C4P2_KarskB in one level file; every entry uses the level key L_C4P2_KarskA, ChapterExt.level_key). `scene` names the walk area and Story scene that reaches the find (read by Game.memory_scenes for the memory cards and by tests/test_c4p2_explore.gd): the back yard and the coal stage x < 858 = L_C4P2_KarskA (Alexei, Monday dawn, open until c4e_inspect_notice; the chat with Maria after c4e_talk_maria), the showcase and platform 1 x > 898 = L_C4P2_KarskB (Alexei, Tuesday evening, open after c4e_inspect_notice; the chat with Lev after c4g_inspect_card until c4g_choose). Inside a memory the remembered scene decides (scripts/ui/minigames/lever_spot.gd). Mini-game „Die Drehscheibe“ (scenes/ui/minigames/Turntable.tscn) at exp_turntable: the press minder wants the sooty shunting engine out of the photograph, the turntable man plays tuba in the band. Side task „Ein Paket über die Linie“ (karsk.task.parcel, Alexei, every step in walk area B): the grandmother on platform 1 (chain on exp_task_parcel: ask -> letter), the sack scale in the sand-drying house (exp_task_scale), the signal wire at the foot of Alexei's own signal (exp_task_wire), the sleeping-car conductor (exp_task_conductor) — no reward but her face. Real-history cards: hist.soviet.propiska at the duty board, hist.soviet.foreign_correspondents in the chat with the press minder. Texts: data/locale/de_explore_c4p2.json; hotspots: assets/environments/karsk_c4p2/explore_hotspots.json. Order = position along the floor (x).",
